        'Total operating expenses':{ t:'Guided to low double digits (cc, ex-inorganic)', h:'<p>Q3 operating expense growth guided to <b>low double digits</b>, currency-neutral and excluding inorganic activity and special items, with a <b>0.5-point</b> headwind from inorganic activity and foreign exchange a tailwind of <b>zero to 0.5 points</b>. For the full year: low double digits, minimal inorganic, a 0.5 to 1 point FX headwind. BVNK, expected to close in Q3, adds some operating expense.</p>' },
        'EPS':{ t:'Other income and expense about $125M; tax 20% to 21%', h:'<p>Q3 other income and expense was guided to an expense of about <b>$125 million</b>, higher than the prior quarter on interest from the June bond issuance, excluding gains and losses on equity investments. The non-GAAP tax rate is guided to <b>20% to 21%</b> for both Q3 and Q4. EPS here is Bloomberg’s GAAP-comparable line, so it reads below the adjusted figure the company quotes ($5.04 in Q2 against $4.97).</p>' },
        'Income tax expense':{ t:'Rate guided to 20% to 21%', h:'<p>Non-GAAP tax rate of <b>20% to 21%</b> for Q3 and Q4. Q1 carried a lower rate on discrete share-based-payment benefits, which do not repeat.</p>' },
        'Share repurchases':{ t:'The accelerated pace carries on', h:'<p>$4.9B repurchased in Q2 and about <b>$700M</b> more through Jul 27, after $4.0B in Q1 plus $1.7B through Apr 27. The pace was raised in Q1 on valuation and conviction in long-term growth. EPS in Q2 included <b>$0.14</b> from buybacks.</p>' },
